d":"chicken","loc":"Maki Leicester Ltd","code":"M11","site":"Leicester","region":"midlands","type":"Out of spec","headline":"1 of 1 readings over the 4.0 to 5.0 window","detail":"mean 6.0, 0 under, 1 over"},{"sev":"high","rank":3,"kind":"chicken","loc":"Maki Leicester Ltd","code":"M11","site":"Leicester","region":"midlands","type":"Outlier vs estate","headline":"mean 6.0 against an estate average of 4.47","detail":"2.7 standard deviations above the group"},{"sev":"high","rank":3,"kind":"pork","loc":"Maki Manchester LTD","code":"M9","site":"Manchester","region":"midlands","type":"Out of spec","headline":"1 of 1 readings under the 6.0 to 7.0 window","detail":"mean 5.6, 1 under, 0 over"},{"sev":"high","rank":3,"kind":"chicken","loc":"Maki Nottingham Ltd","code":"M16","site":"Nottingham","region":"midlands","type":"Flatline","headline":"exactly 5.0 on every one of 14 readings over 14 days","detail":"no variation at all over a fortnight, so the meter is probably not being used"},{"sev":"med","rank":2,"kind":"pork","loc":"Maki Manchester LTD","code":"M9","site":"Manchester","region":"midlands","type":"Outlier vs estate","headline":"mean 5.6 against an estate average of 6.34","detail":"1.6 standard deviations below the group"}],"resolution":{"whole_only":30,"lines":38,"pct":78.9,"note":"Most of the estate only ever records whole numbers. A refractometer reads to one decimal, so a whole number is a rounded number. On a window only 1.0 or 2.0 wide, rounding to the nearest whole unit is a big fraction of the tolerance and it hides small drifts entirely. Sites already reporting decimals prove the meters can do it."},"cases":[{"loc":"Maki Nottingham Ltd","code":"M16","site":"Nottingham","region":"midlands","kind":"chicken","priority":"P1","when":"this week","headline":"Not measuring","response":"Unannounced visit. Watch the check being taken, then take it yourself on the same pot and compare. If the refractometer is missing, broken or uncalibrated, replace it before anything else. Do not treat this as a broth problem until a real reading exists.","evidence":"one DEC-witnessed reading, plus 5 consecutive days of varying readings after","owner":"Matt Polak (Executive Chef) (escalated from Artur Mroczkowski)","mean":5.0,"in_spec_pct":100.0,"under":0,"over":0,"missed":0,"flags":["Flatline"],"flag_count":1,"runs_open":2,"first_seen":"2026-10-18","escalated":true,"owner_original":"Artur Mroczkowski (DEC North England & Midlands)","escalation_note":"open for 2 consecutive runs, escalated to the Executive Chef"},{"loc":"Maki Manchester LTD","code":"M9","site":"Manchester","region":"midlands","kind":"pork","priority":"P1","when":"this week","headline":"Consistently too weak","response":"Method check at the pass, then a service check. Too weak is either over-watering at make-up or topping the pot up during service. Watch both. If they are topping up, that is a par and prep-quantity problem, not a recipe problem.","evidence":"7 consecutive readings inside 6.0 to 7.0","owner":"Matt Polak (Executive Chef) (escalated from Artur Mroczkowski)","mean":5.6,"in_spec_pct":0.0,"under":1,"over":0,"missed":0,"flags":["Out of spec","Outlier vs estate"],"flag_count":2,"runs_open":2,"first_seen":"2026-10-18","escalated":true,"owner_original":"Artur Mroczkowski (DEC North England & Midlands)","escalation_note":"open for 2 consecutive runs, escalated to the Executive Chef"},{"loc":"Maki Leicester Ltd","code":"M11","site":"Leicester","region":"midlands","kind":"chicken","priority":"P1","when":"this week","headline":"Consistently too strong","response":"Method check at the pass. Watch one batch made start to finish: what vessel is the water measured with, and is the ratio the current spec? Too strong almost always means under-watering a concentrate. Re-read with the chef present and agree the ratio in writing before you leave.","evidence":"7 consecutive readings inside 4.0 to 5.0","owner":"Artur Mroczkowski (DEC North England & Midlands)","mean":6.0,"in_spec_pct":0.0,"under":0,"over":1,"missed":0,"flags":["Out of spec","Outlier vs estate"],"flag_count":2,"runs_open":1,"first_seen":"2026-10-19","escalated":false}],"estate_actions":[{"id":"mapal-comparer","priority":"P1","owner":"Michael / Ross","title":"Set the Mapal comparer to the real windows","why":"Mapal catches 1 of 2 out-of-spec readings and misses 1. It has no upper limit configured at all, and over-strength is now essentially the whole problem.","do":"Change the Chicken Broth Check comparer to 4.0-5.0 and the Tonkotsu Broth Check to 6.0-7.0. Every one of those misses then raises itself as a deviation at the point of failure, on the chef's screen, with a corrective action required.","effect":"turns this whole page from a fortnightly report into a live control"},{"id":"decimals","priority":"P2","owner":"Michael / Ross","title":"Require one decimal place on both broth checks","why":"30 of 38 site lines (78.9%) only ever record whole numbers, on windows just 1.0 wide. A site writing 5 on a 4 to 5 chicken window is sitting exactly on the ceiling, and small drifts are invisible.","do":"Set the answer option to one decimal, and say so in the task text.","effect":"makes the window usable and the drift detectable"},{"id":"factory-spec","priority":"P2","owner":"Ross","title":"Set a factory target band","why":"The factory has no spec, so it can only be scored on steadiness. It could slide from 8.30 to 7.60 over a month, smoothly, and keep scoring in the 90s.","do":"Give a min and max for factory tonkotsu and chicken after ice.","effect":"the factory panel scores against a target instead of just measuring steadiness"}],"week":{"monday":"2026-10-19","days":["2026-10-19"],"partial":true}}